01:22:01.695 --> 01:22:06.645
[MUSIC PLAYING]

01:29:59.938 --> 01:30:03.920
[APPLAUSE]

01:30:03.920 --> 01:30:07.220
Ben Hart on tenor
saxophone, Dylan Sleeper

01:30:07.220 --> 01:30:14.300
on tenor saxophone, Kevin
Costello on the trombone.

01:30:14.300 --> 01:30:18.870
And our three percussionists
David, Miguel, Jorge.

01:30:26.370 --> 01:30:27.700
Thank you so much, everyone.

01:30:27.700 --> 01:30:29.190
Thank you, Fred and the band.

01:30:29.190 --> 01:30:32.160
It's really just
a privilege always

01:30:32.160 --> 01:30:33.930
to collaborate with
Fred and everyone

01:30:33.930 --> 01:30:37.350
here at MIT and this
amazing group of musicians.

01:30:37.350 --> 01:30:39.780
They've been working
hard on this music

01:30:39.780 --> 01:30:41.190
for the past couple of months.

01:30:41.190 --> 01:30:44.820
And it's just really inspiring
to be here and get to finally

01:30:44.820 --> 01:30:48.000
have it played and then have you
all here to share this moment

01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:49.480
with us is really meaningful.

01:30:49.480 --> 01:30:53.040
So thank you so much for being
here and supporting the cause.

01:30:53.040 --> 01:30:59.017
I really have to
acknowledge Fred's work

01:30:59.017 --> 01:30:59.850
through all of this.

01:30:59.850 --> 01:31:06.120
He's really been the brains
behind this whole operation.

01:31:06.120 --> 01:31:08.910
He reached out to me, I want
to say, maybe a couple of years

01:31:08.910 --> 01:31:14.130
ago about bringing this
band down to the island

01:31:14.130 --> 01:31:16.710
and doing various
activities there

01:31:16.710 --> 01:31:20.280
from concerts to
educational activities,

01:31:20.280 --> 01:31:21.910
cultural exchanges, et cetera.

01:31:21.910 --> 01:31:24.390
And we've been planning
this trip for a while.

01:31:24.390 --> 01:31:26.970
Obviously, it had to be
postponed for obvious reasons.

01:31:26.970 --> 01:31:29.730
But Fred was the
one that was really

01:31:29.730 --> 01:31:32.340
pushing hard about having
this concert tonight.

01:31:32.340 --> 01:31:35.790
We're going to have the same
concert in New York tomorrow.

01:31:35.790 --> 01:31:38.530
Really more than
anything else, we're

01:31:38.530 --> 01:31:41.640
just trying to create awareness
about the situation that's

01:31:41.640 --> 01:31:43.240
still going on in Puerto Rico.

01:31:43.240 --> 01:31:45.600
I mean, you saw all that
footage from earlier.

01:31:45.600 --> 01:31:48.570
It was very, very
powerful footage.

01:31:48.570 --> 01:31:51.000
But it's really sad to
say that that's still

01:31:51.000 --> 01:31:53.290
going on in certain
parts of Puerto Rico.

01:31:53.290 --> 01:31:55.980
There's folks without
water, without electricity,

01:31:55.980 --> 01:32:00.090
without very, very
basic everyday needs.

01:32:00.090 --> 01:32:02.850
And they really need
all the help they get.

01:32:02.850 --> 01:32:05.047
There's a lot of stuff
going on in the world,

01:32:05.047 --> 01:32:07.380
a lot of stuff going on in
this country, in our country,

01:32:07.380 --> 01:32:08.730
and Puerto Rico also.

01:32:08.730 --> 01:32:12.660
So it's easy for
this to be all news

01:32:12.660 --> 01:32:15.060
because it happened five
months ago, six months ago.

01:32:15.060 --> 01:32:18.960
But you should know that
it's still going on.

01:32:18.960 --> 01:32:21.240
There's still a
lot of need there.

01:32:21.240 --> 01:32:24.570
There's still a lot
of chaos unfortunately

01:32:24.570 --> 01:32:25.710
going on in the island.

01:32:25.710 --> 01:32:29.190
So we're just trying to
really create awareness

01:32:29.190 --> 01:32:30.930
for folks like
yourselves and everyone

01:32:30.930 --> 01:32:35.700
out there who's listening that
anything you can do to help

01:32:35.700 --> 01:32:39.840
is greatly needed and I'm
sure is greatly appreciated

01:32:39.840 --> 01:32:41.382
by the folks down there.

01:32:41.382 --> 01:32:42.840
This last piece
we're going to play

01:32:42.840 --> 01:32:45.180
is a piece I wrote
specifically for tonight.

01:32:45.180 --> 01:32:48.480
It's the first time we've
ever played it in public.

01:32:48.480 --> 01:32:50.610
We rehearsed it for the
last couple of days.

01:32:50.610 --> 01:32:55.535
And I wrote this piece
thinking about various things.

01:32:58.530 --> 01:33:02.040
One of the main things
that's happened-- it

01:33:02.040 --> 01:33:04.920
was also already happening
before the disaster.

01:33:04.920 --> 01:33:07.898
But especially after
the hurricanes hit,

01:33:07.898 --> 01:33:09.690
a lot of Puerto Ricans
just started leaving

01:33:09.690 --> 01:33:11.290
the island for obvious reasons.

01:33:11.290 --> 01:33:13.600
Some of them, they
didn't have a home.

01:33:13.600 --> 01:33:16.530
They needed medical help.

01:33:16.530 --> 01:33:18.810
They needed a job.

01:33:18.810 --> 01:33:22.830
So they started migrating to
the United States and elsewhere.

01:33:22.830 --> 01:33:25.510
But a lot of people
did stay on the island.

01:33:25.510 --> 01:33:29.520
And they kind of
grinded through it.

01:33:29.520 --> 01:33:31.260
And they're still
grinding through it.

01:33:31.260 --> 01:33:35.580
I have a lot of friends from
artists to most small business

01:33:35.580 --> 01:33:38.730
owners who decided to stay
there and do what they could

01:33:38.730 --> 01:33:42.210
to build that country back up.

01:33:42.210 --> 01:33:44.940
So I wrote this piece for
them thinking about them

01:33:44.940 --> 01:33:47.215
and thinking about the
resiliency and the courage

01:33:47.215 --> 01:33:48.840
of a lot of those
people in Puerto Rico

01:33:48.840 --> 01:33:50.923
and a lot of the people
who are trying to help out

01:33:50.923 --> 01:33:52.180
the situation there.

01:33:52.180 --> 01:33:53.840
And this one is called
En Pie de Lucha.

01:33:53.840 --> 01:33:55.465
This is going to
close out the concert.

01:33:55.465 --> 01:33:56.460
So thank you very much.

01:33:56.460 --> 01:33:57.668
Thank you for your attention.

01:33:57.668 --> 01:34:02.440
[APPLAUSE]

